cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BELFEM in academic work, please cite the paper below
  (preferred-citation). The DOI record carries the complete author list.
type: software
title: "BELFEM: Berkeley Lab Finite Element Framework"
abstract: >-
  A special-purpose C++17 finite element framework for high-performance
  computing, focused on the magnetodynamic modeling of high-temperature
  superconductors: h-phi formulation with thin-shell elements, automatically
  generated cohomology cuts, coupled thermal and lumped-circuit physics, and
  MPI-parallel sparse direct solvers.
authors:
  - family-names: Messe
    given-names: Christian
    affiliation: Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    BELFEM: a special purpose finite element code for the magnetodynamic
    modeling of high-temperature superconductor tapes
  authors:
